  "output": "**Verification status: NOT PERFORMABLE — no draft was provided in this session.**\n\nI have to report this plainly rather than produce a review, because the review task cannot be honestly completed:\n\n**What is missing**\n\n1. **The draft itself.** No draft text was included in the message or attached to this session. There are no sentences, claims, or citation markers to check.\n2. **The retrieved content.** No source material, search results, or documents were retrieved or passed into this session. There is no corpus against which factual statements could be grounded.\n\n**Why I will not fabricate a review**\n\nProducing a \"verification report\" here would require inventing both the draft's claims and the sources they allegedly cite. That would be a worse violation of the exact standard the review is meant to enforce — grounding every statement in actually retrieved content and mapping every citation to a real source. A fabricated audit is indistinguishable from the failure mode it audits against.\n\n**The protocol I would apply once the draft is supplied** (documented so the process is on record):\n\n- **Claim-by-claim grounding check:** extract every factual assertion from the draft and match it to a specific passage in the retrieved content; flag any statement supported only by my prior knowledge rather than a retrieved source.\n- **Citation-to-source mapping:** verify each `[n]` marker corresponds to a source that was actually retrieved, and that the cited source actually supports the specific claim it is attached to (not merely a related topic).\n- **Overreach detection:** flag claims that stretch beyond what the source snippet states (e.g., causation implied where a source shows correlation, generalization beyond the studied population).\n- **Stale or absent-date checks:** flag quantitative claims (figures, dates, statistics) lacking a retrievable source or a date consistent with today's date (2026-09-25).\n- **Output format:** a table or annotated listing — claim → source → verdict (grounded / partially grounded / unsupported / citation mismatch).\n\n**Bottom line:** Nothing can be verified because nothing was provided. If the draft text and the retrieved source set are supplied in a subsequent message, the review above can be executed directly. Until then, the only honest finding is: **0 claims checked, 0 citations checked — insufficient material to perform the audit.**",
